  "fig.vs.supply.box": "{supply}; how many are sold is encrypted",
  "fig.vs.supply.rat": "{maxSeed} random and {maxModel} AI, {perWallet} per wallet",
  "fig.vs.earns": "Earns",
  "fig.vs.earns.box": "A bag of {bag} cCROQ, then 0 to {max} a day, hidden in the box",
  "fig.vs.earns.rat": "{perDay} plain CROQ a day, to its owner",
  "fig.vs.markets": "Wallets and markets",
  "fig.vs.markets.box": "Need a market built for the confidential ERC-721, like the flea market",
  "fig.vs.markets.rat": "A standard ERC-721: any wallet or market can show it",
  "fig.vs.secret": "Its secret",
  "fig.vs.secret.box": "The cat, who holds it, what it earns",
  "fig.vs.secret.rat": "Its power (1, 2 or 3), read by its holder only",
  "docs.rats.p1": "A rat you like in the studio can be adopted: minted as an NFT of your own in the Rats contract, paid in plain USDC straight to the collection's treasury. A random rat costs {seed} USDC and is adopted by its seed, each seed once: its look is worked out from that number again wherever it is shown, so there is nothing else to store. An AI rat costs {model} USDC: its picture is first stored on Arweave for good, like the cats' pictures, while its 3D model is kept by the game's server.",
  "docs.rats.p2": "There will only ever be {maxSeed} random rats and {maxModel} AI rats, set for good in the contract, and one wallet adopts {perWallet} at most, both kinds together. A rat can still be given or sold to a wallet past that. The studio and the home page show how many are left.",
  "docs.rats.p3": "A rat is everything a box is not, on purpose: the cats are the depot's secret residents, the rats its open ones. Who owns a rat and what it looks like are public, so it works like any NFT. It keeps one secret only: its power, below.",
  "docs.rats.h.croq": "A rat's croquettes",
  "docs.rats.p4": "Each rat earns {perDay} plain CROQ a day from the day it was adopted. They come from the rats' own pantry, the RatPantry, which got {fund} CROQ from the treasury, and not from the Pantry that feeds the boxes: the rats never touch the game reserve. Collect them from \"My rats\" in the game, for all your rats at once. A rat keeps {maxDays} days at most between two collections; left alone longer, it earns nothing more. If the pantry is ever empty, collecting fails and the days wait; when it runs low, it pays what is left. The croquettes are plain because a rat's owner is public anyway: there is nothing to hide in what it earns. Sealed at the bureau de change, they can feed a cat.",
  "docs.rats.h.sniff": "Sniffing the boxes",
  "docs.rats.p5": "A rat also sniffs. In \"My rats\", type the number of a sealed box you do not hold and press Sniff: your rat tells you one of its traits, for your eyes only. It is a paid shake, 2.5 cUSDC: 70% waits in the box for its holder, 30% goes to the treasury, and everyone else only sees that a rat sniffed that box. A power-1 rat gets 0.75 cUSDC of it back from the treasury, in secret: nobody can tell which rats sniff cheaper.",
  "docs.rats.p6": "That is how a rat helps before a purchase: a few sniffs of a box you are thinking of buying, and you know as much about it as the seller did.",
  "docs.rats.h.power": "A secret power",
  "docs.rats.p7": "Every rat gets a secret power when it is adopted, random or AI, bought or given: 1, 2 or 3, drawn under encryption, so nobody, the team included, can choose or predict it. Only its holder can read it: in \"My rats\", press Read it. If you buy a rat, the first reading asks your wallet once for the right to read it; the seller keeps knowing what it was.",
  "docs.rats.h.tricks": "Protect or attack a box",
  "docs.rats.p8": "A rat can also be set on a sealed box for {days} days; then it rests {rest} days before it can go again. Type the box's number in \"My rats\", pick the trait to block (it only counts for a power-2 rat), and set it on the box. What it does depends on whose box it is, and the contract works that out by itself, in secret:",
  "docs.rats.p9": "On one of your own boxes, it protects it. Whoever pays to shake it, or sends a rat to sniff it, reads a fake for the traits your rat blocks: the same fake every time, so it looks real. You still read the truth. Before a sale, that keeps your box's best traits to yourself.",
  "docs.rats.p10": "On someone else's box, it attacks it. When its holder shakes their own box, the traits your rat blocks come back scrambled for {days} days. They learn that someone jams them, never who. A box protected by a power-3 rat resists attacks.",
  "docs.rats.p11": "Every rat has the same button, the same {days} days and the same rest, so the chain only shows \"rat 12 sat on box 340\": not whether it protected or attacked, not its power, not which trait. A power-1 rat set on a box does nothing at all: a perfect bluff. Duels are not affected: the trait a loser shows is always the true one.",
  "fig.powers.aria": "The three powers a rat can have, how often each comes, and what each does",
